# Line endings.
#
# Biome is configured to format with LF, and `biome ci` fails on a CRLF file. On
# Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites files to CRLF on every checkout — and
# lint-staged stashes and restores around each commit, which counts as a checkout.
# Without this file the pre-commit hook therefore reintroduces CRLF into working
# files on every commit and the next `biome ci` fails, on a clean tree, for
# reasons that look like nothing to do with the change being made.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository *and* checks out LF
# regardless of the contributor's autocrlf setting, so the formatter and git agree
# on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep CRLF to work on Windows.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch these, and do not try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary

# Generated: collapsed by default in GitHub reviews.
#
# Deliberately NOT marked `-diff`. That would make git treat it as binary, which
# hides the content entirely — and a lockfile diff is exactly what you want to
# read when checking whether an install pulled in something unexpected.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
